From: steamac <steamac@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] ALSA: virtio: reset partly filled periods on prepare

Since "ALSA: virtio: use ack callback" the driver enqueues a playback
message only once the application has filled its whole period
(msg->length == period_bytes), and msg->length is only cleared when the
device completes the message. ops->prepare() resets hw_ptr, msg_count and
the pcm_indirect state but not the message lengths, so a period that was
partly filled when the stream stopped (an xrun, or a drop by an
application such as PipeWire whose quantum is not a multiple of the
period) keeps its stale length. After the restart that period overshoots
period_bytes on its next fill, is never enqueued again, and the device
never sees it: hw_ptr falls one period behind the application pointer per
buffer cycle until the buffer is full, and the stream stalls for good
while staying RUNNING (seen with PipeWire, 128-frame periods: playback
hangs about 0.6 s after the restart, avail = 1 period).

Clear every message's length in ops->prepare(), together with the rest
of the per-run state.
---
--- a/sound/virtio/virtio_pcm.h
+++ b/sound/virtio/virtio_pcm.h
@@ -118,6 +118,8 @@
 
 void virtsnd_pcm_msg_free(struct virtio_pcm_substream *vss);
 
+void virtsnd_pcm_msg_reset(struct virtio_pcm_substream *vss);
+
 int virtsnd_pcm_msg_send(struct virtio_pcm_substream *vss, unsigned long offset,
 			 unsigned long bytes);
 
--- a/sound/virtio/virtio_pcm_msg.c
+++ b/sound/virtio/virtio_pcm_msg.c
@@ -183,6 +183,31 @@
 }
 
 /**
+ * virtsnd_pcm_msg_reset() - Forget the fill level of all I/O messages.
+ * @vss: VirtIO PCM substream.
+ *
+ * A message is only enqueued once the application has filled its whole
+ * period (msg->length == period_bytes), and the length is only cleared when
+ * the device completes the message. A period that was partly filled when the
+ * substream stopped (e.g. on an xrun, or a drop by an application writing in
+ * chunks that are not a multiple of the period) therefore kept its stale
+ * length across ops->prepare(): after the restart that period overshoots
+ * period_bytes, is never enqueued again, and the substream stalls once the
+ * device has played everything else (hw_ptr stops one period short of the
+ * application pointer per buffer cycle until the buffer is full).
+ *
+ * Context: Process context, no I/O messages pending.
+ */
+void virtsnd_pcm_msg_reset(struct virtio_pcm_substream *vss)
+{
+	unsigned int i;
+
+	guard(spinlock_irqsave)(&vss->lock);
+	for (i = 0; vss->msgs && i < vss->nmsgs; ++i)
+		vss->msgs[i]->length = 0;
+}
+
+/**
  * virtsnd_pcm_msg_send() - Send asynchronous I/O messages.
  * @vss: VirtIO PCM substream.
  * @offset: starting position that has been updated
--- a/sound/virtio/virtio_pcm_ops.c
+++ b/sound/virtio/virtio_pcm_ops.c
@@ -299,6 +299,7 @@
 	vss->xfer_xrun = false;
 	vss->suspended = false;
 	vss->msg_count = 0;
+	virtsnd_pcm_msg_reset(vss);
 
 	memset(&vss->pcm_indirect, 0, sizeof(vss->pcm_indirect));
 	vss->pcm_indirect.sw_buffer_size =
